{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.TopologicalMass","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.TopologicalMass","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Projection","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.idempotent_gives_mass_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.idempotent_gives_mass_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L133-L140","doc":"The idempotent decomposition produces a valid MassDecomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.descended_trace_is_base_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.descended_trace_is_base_level","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L118-L131","doc":"The descended trace equals the trace of the base-level cycle γ₀,\nbecause τₙ projects onto im(ℓₙ) ≅ End_𝒞(Aₙ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.mass_decomposition_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.mass_decomposition_exact","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L106-L116","doc":"**Exact mass decomposition** under non-negativity of traces:\nm(γ) = m_desc(γ) + m_trans(γ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.norm_additivity_of_nonneg_traces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.norm_additivity_of_nonneg_traces","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L77-L104","doc":"**Norm additivity for non-negative traces**: when both the descended\nand transient trace values are non-negative — as guaranteed by the\nFrobenius pairing in the archimedean realisation, where trace values\nare norms of holonomies — the mass decomposes exactly (not just as\nan upper bound).\n\nFor `R = ℝ`, this is provable from non-negativity alone, eliminating\nthe need for an axiom.  The original product-zero hypothesis\n(`descendedTrace * transientTrace = 0`) was mathematically incorrect:\nin a `NormedCommRing` without zero divisors (such as `ℝ`) it forces\none component to vanish (making the decomposition vacuous), and in\nrings with zero divisors it does not imply norm additivity.\n\nThe correct physical content is that both trace components are\nnon-negative reals: the descended trace is `‖Hol_{∇_A}(γ₀)‖ ≥ 0`\nand each transient trace is `‖Φ_q(zᵢ)‖ ≥ 0`.  For non-negative\nreals, `‖a + b‖ = |a + b| = a + b = |a| + |b| = ‖a‖ + ‖b‖`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.mass_upper_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.mass_upper_bound","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L58-L75","doc":"**Topological Decomposition of Mass** (trace-level):\n\nFrom the algebraic decomposition `tr = tr_desc + tr_trans`,\nthe mass decomposes as:\n`m(γ) = ‖tr_desc + tr_trans‖`\n\nThe triangle inequality gives:\n`m(γ) ≤ ‖tr_desc‖ + ‖tr_trans‖`\n\nThis is always valid. Equality holds when the descended and transient\ncomponents are \"Frobenius-orthogonal\" (norm-additive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The total trace decomposes as descended + transient.\nThis follows from the idempotent splitting: any x decomposes\nas τ(x) + (x - τ(x)), so tr(x) = tr(τ(x)) + tr(x - τ(x)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.totalTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.totalTrace","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The total cycle trace value (before decomposition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.transientTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.transientTrace","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The transient trace: tr restricted to 𝒜^trans = ker(τ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.descendedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.descendedTrace","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The descended trace: tr restricted to 𝒜^desc = im(τ). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L44-L56","doc":"Decomposition data: the descended and transient trace contributions,\nderived from an idempotent splitting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.categoricalMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.categoricalMass","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The categorical mass of a cycle, defined as ‖tr((λ ⊗ id) ∘ Δ ∘ γ)‖. ","signatureChunk":0}]}